Testimony — Grace Alvarez, Quezon City, Philippines (age 33)
“I called my panic ‘prudence.’ I checked the exchange rate before prayer, doom-scrolled before breakfast, and drafted worst-case scenarios during worship. Chest tightness became nightly. One dawn I read Matthew 6:25–34 out loud until the sun rose (full text: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+6%3A25-34&version=ESV
). The words hit like a verdict: My worry was disobedience.

“King Jesus, I renounce the idol of worry and the spirit of fear. I confess that anxiety is disobedience to Your command. I cast these specific cares into Your hands now: [say them one by one]. I choose to seek first Your kingdom and Your righteousness (Matthew 6:33 — full: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+6%3A33&version=ESV
). I receive Your peace that surpasses understanding (Philippians 4:6–7 — full: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Philippians+4%3A6-7&version=ESV
). I humble myself under Your mighty hand and cast all my anxieties on You (1 Peter 5:7 — full: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+Peter+5%3A7&version=ESV).”
